    "“Only use AI that runs on this Mac” is on, and the AI source you chose sends questions elsewhere, so nothing was asked. Turn the switch off under Settings › Privacy, or choose Apple Intelligence or a server on this Mac under Settings › General › AI." : {},
    "“contact” and a name finds people in your Contacts. macOS asks first, and only once you type that word and a name. Nothing is saved." : {},
    "“event” and a sentence adds an event to your default calendar. macOS asks first, and the event’s receipt deletes it again." : {},
    "“kill” and a name, or “port” and a number, lists your running processes. The list is read when you ask and is not kept." : {},
    "“note” makes a Markdown file here and “append” adds a line to the day’s note. Obsidian and Octarine read the same files." : {},
    "“remind” and a sentence adds a reminder. Floe reads the names of your lists and none of your reminders." : {},
    "↵ Open" : {},
    "⌘Y Quick Look" : {},
    "⌘⇧C Copy Path" : {},
    "⌘⇧C copies details · Esc goes back" : {}
